ing South Fork and\nMogote.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a86d832769b4b479ba2fd2815cb3755bcf6b1d9a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a86d832769b4b479ba2fd2815cb3755bcf6b1d9a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 31 at 1:59PM MDT until November 4 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will be possible,\nespecially over the western half of San Luis Valley.\n\n* WHERE...The western half of the San Luis Valley, including\nAntonito, Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone location.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-04T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a86d832769b4b479ba2fd2815cb3755bcf6b1d9a.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a86d832769b4b479ba2fd2815cb3755bcf6b1d9a.002.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued October 31 at 11:03AM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Hea